{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jas-3-1","title":"James 3:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 We are not rashly or arrogantly to reprove others; 5 but rather to bridle the tongue, a little member, but a powerful instrument of much good, and great harm. 13 They who are truly wise are mild and peaceable without envying and strife.</p>\n<p>be. Mal 2:12; Mt 9:11; 10:24; 23:8-10,14; Joh 3:10; Ac 13:1; Ro 2:20,21 1Co 12:28; Eph 4:11; 1Ti 2:7; 2Ti 1:11; *Gr: 1Pe 5:3 knowing. Le 10:3; Eze 3:17,18; 33:7-9; Lu 6:37; 12:47,48; 16:2; Ac 20:26,27 1Co 4:2-5; 2Co 5:10; Heb 13:17 condemnation. or, judgement. Mt 7:1,2; 23:14; 1Co 11:29-32; *Gr:</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-3-2","title":"James 3:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>in. 1Ki 8:46; 2Ch 6:36; Pr 20:9; Ec 7:20; Isa 64:6; Ro 3:10; 7:21 Ga 3:22; 5:17; 1Jo 1:8-10 If. 5,6; 1:26; Ps 34:13; Pr 13:3; 1Pe 3:10 a perfect. 1:4; Mt 12:37; Col 1:28; 4:12; Heb 13:21; 1Pe 5:10 to bridle. 1Co 9:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-3-3","title":"James 3:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>1:26; 2Ki 19:28; Ps 32:9; 39:1; Isa 37:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-3-4","title":"James 3:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>are driven. Ps 107:25-27; Jon 1:4; Mt 8:24; Ac 27:14-38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-3-5","title":"James 3:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>so. Ex 5:2; 15:9; 2Ki 19:22-24; Job 21:14,15; 22:17; Ps 10:3; 12:2-4 Ps 17:10; 52:1,2; 73:8,9; Pr 12:18; 15:2; 18:21; Jer 9:3-8; 18:18 Eze 28:2; 29:3; Da 3:15; 4:30; 2Pe 2:18; Jude 1:16; Re 13:5,6 matter. or, wood.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas